{"id":3866,"date":"2024-09-13T08:47:06","date_gmt":"2024-09-12T23:17:06","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/feedops.com\/?p=3866"},"modified":"2024-09-26T16:54:58","modified_gmt":"2024-09-26T07:24:58","slug":"sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/","title":{"rendered":"Sales vs. Advertising in E-commerce: Why the Difference Matters"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"3866\" class=\"elementor elementor-3866\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3e8c2ab e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"3e8c2ab\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9489eb4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"9489eb4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Sales vs. Advertising in E-commerce: How I Got it Wrong!<\/h2><p>About twenty years ago, I attended a marketing conference that highlighted the battle between sales vs. advertising in e-commerce. A senior executive, speaking with confidence, presented a beautifully designed slide and declared, &#8216;Half of my advertising is wasted. The problem is, I don\u2019t know which half.<\/p><p>At that time, I was a confident digital marketer. During a break, I approached him and said, \u201cI know exactly which half is wasted because I\u2019m in digital.\u201d Little did I know how wrong I was.<\/p><p>It wasn\u2019t until a decade later, after managing countless campaigns for my e-commerce clients, that I realized the truth. What I was doing wasn\u2019t really advertising\u2014it was selling. And in e-commerce, the distinction between sales and advertising is critical.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-97f11da e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"97f11da\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-724f1b6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"724f1b6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">The E-commerce Conundrum: Selling or Advertising?<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3402ed2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"3402ed2\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Running an e-commerce business requires a clear understanding of where your marketing efforts are focused. Are you driving direct sales, or are you working to build brand awareness? Early in my career, I often confused the two. I ran campaigns thinking they were for brand-building, but in reality, they were focused on immediate sales.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6d26112 elementor-widget-divider--view-line elementor-widget elementor-widget-divider\" data-id=\"6d26112\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"divider.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-divider\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-divider-separator\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/span>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-aea8a13 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"aea8a13\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6557347 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6557347\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Want to dive deeper into the difference between sales and advertising? Check out this video from my <a href=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/learning\/\">Learning Hub<\/a>,\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/masterclass\/\">Masterclass series,<\/a> where I explain the key distinctions and why they matter for e-commerce success.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f203597 elementor-widget elementor-widget-video\" data-id=\"f203597\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-settings=\"{&quot;youtube_url&quot;:&quot;https:\\\/\\\/www.youtube.com\\\/watch?v=sMWiXp-Y_fw&quot;,&quot;video_type&quot;:&quot;youtube&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;yes&quot;}\" data-widget_type=\"video.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-wrapper elementor-open-inline\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-video\"><\/div>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-de1061a e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"de1061a\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e547ba4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"e547ba4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>The turning point came during a discussion with my fractional CFO, a detail-oriented numbers guy. He pointed out that the campaigns I was running weren\u2019t advertising at all. \u201cLook at the data,\u201d he said. \u201cYou\u2019re spending X dollars and getting Y back. This isn\u2019t advertising\u2014it\u2019s selling.\u201d It was a lightbulb moment for me: in e-commerce, especially when budgets are tight, it\u2019s essential to know whether you\u2019re aiming for quick sales or long-term brand growth.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3079bcd elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"3079bcd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">The Transactional Nature of E-commerce Sales<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-41bd7bb elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"41bd7bb\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>In e-commerce, the sales process is transactional by nature. Tools like Google Shopping, dynamic remarketing, and paid search campaigns are designed to drive conversions. With these tools, you can track every click and purchase, understanding exactly how your spend translates into sales. This clarity is what makes e-commerce so appealing to marketers focused on customer acquisition and driving immediate revenue.<\/p><p>But it\u2019s important to remember that these efforts\u2014while crucial\u2014aren\u2019t the same as traditional advertising. They\u2019re part of a larger sales strategy, designed to push products into customers\u2019 hands, rather than build long-term brand recognition.<\/p><p>I learned this the hard way. When I ran a sales team to acquire clients for my media agency, we focused heavily on closing deals. While these clients stayed with me for years, the acquisition cost was high, and it became clear that focusing solely on sales could jeopardize long-term growth.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-355ecd4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"355ecd4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Google Performance Max: Blurring the Lines Between Sales and Advertising<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-33e6d36 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"33e6d36\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-Vs-Advertising-Pmax-Tug-of-War-.webp\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-4086\" alt=\"Sales Vs Advertising Pmax Tug of War\" srcset=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-Vs-Advertising-Pmax-Tug-of-War-.webp 1024w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-Vs-Advertising-Pmax-Tug-of-War--300x300.webp 300w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-Vs-Advertising-Pmax-Tug-of-War--150x150.webp 150w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-Vs-Advertising-Pmax-Tug-of-War--768x768.webp 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5fae90b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"5fae90b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>The launch of Google\u2019s Performance Max (PMax) has made it even harder to distinguish between sales and advertising. PMax optimizes campaigns across multiple channels\u2014Google Shopping, search, display, and more\u2014making it a powerful tool for e-commerce businesses.<\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p><p>But there\u2019s a catch. While PMax drives immediate sales through platforms like Google Shopping, it also ventures into brand-building territory through predictive audiences and awareness campaigns. Take dynamic remarketing, for example: it reminds potential customers to complete a purchase, pushing them to convert. But PMax also uses the same data to target new, potential customers\u2014an approach that\u2019s more in line with traditional advertising.<\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p><p>For e-commerce brands, this duality can be both exciting and challenging. Are you focusing on closing sales today, or are you laying the groundwork for future growth?<\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e01f5af elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"e01f5af\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Finding the Balance: Sales and Advertising for E-commerce Success<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-99b5367 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"99b5367\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\u00a0<\/p><p><span style=\"text-align: var(--text-align); color: var( --e-global-color-text ); font-size: 1.125rem;\">If you own an e-commerce brand, understanding the difference between sales and advertising is crucial to your strategy. If your primary goal is driving immediate revenue, tools like Google Shopping and dynamic remarketing will help you convert browsers into buyers. These are essential for closing deals and generating quick wins.<\/span><\/p><p>However, if your focus is on long-term growth, traditional advertising strategies are key. This includes building brand awareness, generating demand, and positioning your brand as a leader in your market. While these efforts won\u2019t pay off immediately, they will set the stage for future success.<\/p><p>Before launching your next e-commerce campaign, take a step back and ask yourself: \u201cAm I focused on selling, or am I building my brand?\u201d This distinction will guide your strategy and help you choose the right tools for the job. Understanding the difference between sales and advertising ensures you maximize the return on every dollar spent.<\/p><h3>Conclusion: Clarity Drives Success in E-commerce<\/h3><p>In today\u2019s fast-paced e-commerce world, knowing whether you\u2019re selling or advertising makes all the difference. Tools like Google Shopping and remarketing drive quick results, but if you want to build a brand that endures, you need a broader approach.<\/p><p>As tools like PMax blur the lines between sales and advertising, it\u2019s essential to keep your goals clear. Separate your sales and advertising efforts, track them differently, and understand how each contributes to your overall growth strategy.<\/p><p>Whether you\u2019re chasing short-term sales or building a brand for the future, success in e-commerce depends on knowing exactly what you\u2019re measuring and why.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Sales vs. Advertising in E-commerce: How I Got it Wrong! About twenty years ago, I attended a marketing conference that highlighted the battle between sales vs. advertising in e-commerce. A senior executive, speaking with confidence, presented a beautifully designed slide and declared, &#8216;Half of my advertising is wasted. The problem is, I don\u2019t know which [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":9,"featured_media":4084,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"content-type":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-3866","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-uncategorized"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v26.6 (Yoast SEO v26.6) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Sales Vs. Advertising in E-commerce: Understanding the Difference<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Understand the distinction between sales vs advertising in e-commerce. Learn why it&#039;s crucial for the success of your online business.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Advertising in E-commerce: Finding the Right Strategy\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Discover the importance of advertising in e-commerce and learn how to effectively target your marketing efforts for optimal results.\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"FeedOps\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/feedops\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-09-12T23:17:06+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-09-26T07:24:58+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-VS-Advertising-ecommerce.png\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1260\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"720\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image\/png\" \/>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Frank Grasso\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Sales vs. Advertising in E-commerce: Why the Difference Matters\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Frank Grasso\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"4 minutes\" \/>\n<script type=\"application\/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\/\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"Frank Grasso\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#\/schema\/person\/935d648bb8def3c2afc809a576755608\"},\"headline\":\"Sales vs. Advertising in E-commerce: Why the Difference Matters\",\"datePublished\":\"2024-09-12T23:17:06+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2024-09-26T07:24:58+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/\"},\"wordCount\":897,\"commentCount\":0,\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#organization\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-vs.-advertising-in-ecommerce-.png\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"CommentAction\",\"name\":\"Comment\",\"target\":[\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#respond\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/\",\"name\":\"Sales Vs. Advertising in E-commerce: Understanding the Difference\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#website\"},\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#primaryimage\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-vs.-advertising-in-ecommerce-.png\",\"datePublished\":\"2024-09-12T23:17:06+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2024-09-26T07:24:58+00:00\",\"description\":\"Understand the distinction between sales vs advertising in e-commerce. Learn why it's crucial for the success of your online business.\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#breadcrumb\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"ReadAction\",\"target\":[\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#primaryimage\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-vs.-advertising-in-ecommerce-.png\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/09\/Sales-vs.-advertising-in-ecommerce-.png\",\"width\":1024,\"height\":1024,\"caption\":\"sales vs advertising in e-commerce\"},{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/sales-vs-advertising-in-e-commerce-why-the-difference-matters\/#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Sales vs. Advertising in E-commerce: Why the Difference Matters\"}]},{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#website\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/\",\"name\":\"FeedOps\",\"description\":\"\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#organization\"},\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"SearchAction\",\"target\":{\"@type\":\"EntryPoint\",\"urlTemplate\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/?s={search_term_string}\"},\"query-input\":{\"@type\":\"PropertyValueSpecification\",\"valueRequired\":true,\"valueName\":\"search_term_string\"}}],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#organization\",\"name\":\"FeedOps\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/05\/Feedops-staggered-logo_Final-2-e1653522818889.png\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/05\/Feedops-staggered-logo_Final-2-e1653522818889.png\",\"width\":899,\"height\":929,\"caption\":\"FeedOps\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/\"},\"sameAs\":[\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/feedops\",\"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/company\/feedops\/\",\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/@feedops\"]},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#\/schema\/person\/935d648bb8def3c2afc809a576755608\",\"name\":\"Frank Grasso\",\"image\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/#\/schema\/person\/image\/\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/10729b10d31fe46be449737d0a25a76598f7994e4b44a67056563d0715c3fa71?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/10729b10d31fe46be449737d0a25a76598f7994e4b44a67056563d0715c3fa71?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"caption\":\"Frank Grasso\"},\"description\":\"I\u2019ve managed over $700 million in ad spend, contributing to billions in revenue. I say \\\"contributing\\\" because online success hinges on three key factors: a product people want, a price they\u2019re willing to pay, and timely delivery. The rest is about attention to detail. I'm not your typical digital advertising expert. My background is unconventional. I left school at 14 and worked as a mechanic until I was 33. In 2002, I leveraged my problem-solving skills to launch a $1 million Google Ads campaign for a travel client. This experience taught me how to optimize ad quality and campaign structure to reduce costs. Over time, I witnessed Google\u2019s evolution: from Sponsored Links to AdWords, then Shopping Ads, Smart Shopping, and finally PMax. As Google expanded its digital media dominance, I realized that my agency needed to adapt. That\u2019s when I shifted focus and sold my agency to start FeedOps. At FeedOps, my mission is to help eCommerce businesses sell more products, increase revenue, and reduce ad spend. We focus on relevance, the core of effective digital advertising. By ensuring your product data and ads are highly relevant to user intent, we help you spend less and gain more. Relevance drives everything from higher click-through rates to better conversion rates and lower costs. At FeedOps, we harness this principle to optimize your ads and product data, ensuring you achieve better returns on your advertising investments. My mission is to help advertisers scale their creativity and productivity, and to provide them with the best tools and solutions to reach their target audiences and achieve their goals. I am passionate about leveraging the latest technologies and trends to enhance the capabilities and performance of our software, and to deliver exceptional value and service to our clients. I am also committed to building and nurturing a talented and diverse team of digital marketers and software developers, who share my vision and values of excellence, collaboration, and customer satisfaction.\",\"sameAs\":[\"http:\/\/www.feedops.com\"],\"url\":\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/author\/frank-grasso\/\"}]}<\/script>\n<!-- \/ Yoast SEO Premium plugin. -->","yoast_head_json":{"title":"Sales Vs. Advertising in E-commerce: Understanding the Difference","description":"Understand the distinction between sales vs advertising in e-commerce. Learn why it's crucial for the success of your online business.","robots":{"index":"index","follow":"follow","max-snippet":"max-snippet:-1","max-image-preview":"max-image-prev